 * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 *
 * ctcc/nrf52840 UICR configuration, applied by .ci_scripts/build_sdk.sh to every
 * image it builds for the card - the application AND the Open Bootloader.
 *
 * gpio-as-nreset routes the reset function to a GPIO so the card can be reset over
 * the mPCIe/M.2 PERST# line. This is not a hex record: the property makes the MDK's
 * SystemInit write UICR->PSELRESET and NVIC_SystemReset() once, on the first boot
 * of an image that carries it (system_nrf52.c, via NRF_CONFIG_GPIO_AS_PINRESET).
 * An image built without it never configures the pin.
 *
 * The upstream ctcc board leaves this to the application, so without this overlay
 * a card that has only ever run the standalone Open Bootloader - a stock card
 * waiting for its first image over serial recovery - has no PERST reset until an
 * application has booted once.
 *
 * The reference application also sets the property in its own board overlay
 * (firmware/boards/ctcc_nrf52840.overlay), which keeps a plain `west build` of
 * firmware/ correct on its own; setting the same boolean property twice is a no-op.
 *
 * Not applied to the assembly test: that image is flashed over SWD for
 * qualification and should not write UICR or reset the card under test.
 */

&uicr {
	gpio-as-nreset;
};
